Perceptron Play Alpha
Now design a 2D perceptron! You're given points scattered in a 2D space, labeled as category 0 or category 1. Your task: find w₁, w₂, and b that correctly classify them all.

Your task: Choose weights and bias for a 2D perceptron that separates the categories.

Think about it: In 2D, you're looking for a line that has all one category on one side and all the other category on the other side. Once you find (or imagine) that line, you can express it mathematically using your two weights and your bias.




